# Interpreter-throw closure item 6, the dynamically selected callable (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md;
# steps/defects.md DYNAMIC-CALLEE-STATUS-ABORT; Codex, CORRECTION FABLE-STATUS-20261011-09): a call through a callable
# formal calls whichever method the actual names -- here conv at the second site, whose implicit convert (the
# initializer edge refusing -1) comes back as the selected callee's status and is caught by the caller of the formal
# (before: "lmx: invariant: a callable that cannot throw reported a status", abort).  Exit 7; 1 would mean the callee
# completed; 2 would mean the first site's result leaked.
fn: conv (int: x) int
    int: neg 0 - x
    size_t: s (neg)
    return: x

fn: fine (int: x) int
    return: x + 1

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: op(value)
    ---
    catch: convert ()
        got: 7
return: got

int: first apply(fine 1)
int: r apply(conv 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
